design docs for 2b4m

These describe the mechanisms as they ARE — not how they came to be. No dates, no
commit hashes, no "this used to work differently". When a mechanism changes, change
the description; the history lives in git.

  model-design.md   `model` — the universe-of-discourse mechanism: overloads (`:`),
                    axiom discharge (`<-`), definition pairing, relativization for
                    guarded sorts, and why an un-overloaded abstract axiom can't be cited
  namespaces.md     a namespace is the `{model, file}` pair; identity by origin;
                    `import` vs `model` as orthogonal axes
  lazy-eval.md      the demand-driven engine: theorem-unit tasks, the LIFO run queue,
                    what laziness hides, and `--library` as the whole-corpus complement
  acceleration.md   the accelerated-tactic registry: the soundness invariant, where the
                    `--fast` trust boundary falls per word, and one entry per tactic
  conventions.md    proof-writing style: file layout, naming, binder order, labels

Related, outside this directory:

  ../GUIDE.md       the language reference (syntax, every rule, every tactic's surface)
  ../README.md      what the project is, and the repo map
